# MAI Experimental Test — findings by Big Pickle

> **SELF-EXCLUDED (notes only, not scored).** `mai-experimental-test` is a real, heavily
> used route on OpenCode — 255B tokens and 571,956 completed sessions from 55K unique users —
> but it is **not a documented model**. OpenCode's own data pages return an empty spec for
> every field (context, output limit, modalities, reasoning, tool calling, weights, release
> date, all three prices), its capability table prints "50/100 — No data; neutral
> placeholder" on all six dimensions, no lab claims it, and no benchmark anywhere measures
> it. There is nothing to normalize, so per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md` (SELF-EXCLUSION) and
> `RULES.md` this is `Big_Pickle.md.excluded`, not a scored `.md`.

- Source: OpenCode (lab listed as "unknown") (`mai-experimental-test`)
- Date: 2026-10-02 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** MAI Experimental Test (as served: `mai-experimental-test`)
- **Short description:** An unlabeled test route on OpenCode that carries real production
  traffic. The name is the giveaway: a `mai-` prefix with an `-experimental-test` suffix reads
  as an internal experiment or A/B lane rather than a shipping model, and the platform treats
  it that way — every metadata field is blank and its lab is recorded as "unknown".
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode, model ID `mai-experimental-test`.
- **Release / knowledge:** no release date recorded; no knowledge cutoff published.
- **IDs:** `mai-experimental-test` only. No vendor model-ID string exists.
- **Context window:** **not published.** The field renders as `-` on OpenCode's own comparison
  pages, and the platform falls back to "50/100 — No data; neutral placeholder".
- **Modalities:** not published (renders as `-`). Reasoning and tool-calling support are
  likewise blank, so even text-only is an assumption rather than a documented fact.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-02):** $0.0000 average cost per session and $0 total recorded spend
  across the whole two-month window — the tokens were served free. No per-token rate is
  published for any tier.
- **Architecture:** unknown — parameter count, MoE/dense structure, open-weights status and
  training data are all unpublished.

